From 93a25b9f0e6e3ea6f24a51479454ad31967cfc0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: callan <callanf@nvidia.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:35:08 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 05/38] feat(engine): pause lower-class prefill and yield
 lower-class decodes to protect a class's ITL, off by default

class_scheduling gains itl_target_ms (per class), protect_max_rank and yield_decodes. Each pass,
the slack of the protected classes' decoding requests (90% of their ITL target times tokens made,
less the time since their first token) sets how many lower-class prefill tokens fit (256-token
steps, from the timing model) and, with yield_decodes, how many lower-class decodes may run
(oldest first). protect_max_rank 0 is the JS model's pausePrefill; 1 with yield_decodes and
preempt_max_rank 1 is its batchYield engine side. Counters: prefill_pauses_total,
decode_yields_total.
---
 crates/core/src/engine/config.rs              |  20 ++-
 crates/core/src/engine/scheduler/vllm/core.rs | 144 +++++++++++++++++-
 .../core/src/engine/scheduler/vllm/tests.rs   |  77 ++++++++++
 3 files changed, 238 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

